WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:11.080
The personal grievance provisions of New Zealand’s Employment Relations Act 2000 (ERA) prevent an employer from firing an employee without good cause.
新西兰《2000年雇佣关系法》（ERA）中的个人申诉条款禁止雇主无正当理由解雇雇员。

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.270
Instead, dismissals must be justified.
相反，解雇必须有正当理由。

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:19.000
Employers must both show cause and act in a procedurally fair way.
雇主既要拿出正当理由，又要在程序上公正行事。

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:26.700
Personal grievance procedures were designed to guard the jobs of ordinary workers from “unjustified dismissals”.
个人申诉程序的设计初衷，是保护普通工人的工作，使他们免遭“无正当理由的解雇”。

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:34.960
The premise was that the common law of contract lacked sufficient safeguards for workers against arbitrary conduct by management.
其前提是：普通法中的合同法缺乏足够的保障，无法保护工人免受管理层专断行为的侵害。

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:40.500
Long gone are the days when a boss could simply give an employee contractual notice.
老板只需按合同规定向雇员发出解雇通知就行，这样的日子早已一去不复返了。

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:47.390
But these provisions create difficulties for businesses when applied to highly paid managers and executives.
但这些条款适用于高薪经理和高管时，会给企业带来困难。

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:59.490
As countless boards and business owners will attest, constraining firms from firing poorly performing, high-earning managers is a handbrake on boosting productivity and overall performance.
正如无数董事会和企业主都会证实的那样，限制企业解雇表现不佳的高收入经理，就是给提升生产率和整体业绩拉上了手刹。

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:06.890
The difference between C-grade and A-grade managers may very well be the difference between business success and failure.
C级经理和A级经理之间的差别，很可能就是企业成功与失败之间的差别。

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:11.580
Between preserving the jobs of ordinary workers and losing them.
也就是保住普通工人的工作与丢掉这些工作之间的差别。

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:16.150
Yet mediocrity is no longer enough to justify a dismissal.
然而，平庸已不再足以成为解雇的正当理由。

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:25.000
Consequently—and paradoxically—laws introduced to protect the jobs of ordinary workers may be placing those jobs at risk.
因此，矛盾的是，为保护普通工人的工作而出台的法律，可能正在让这些工作面临风险。

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:39.710
If not placing jobs at risk, to the extent employment protection laws constrain business owners from dismissing under-performing managers, those laws act as a constraint on firm productivity and therefore on workers’ wages.
就算没有让工作面临风险，只要就业保护法限制了企业主解雇表现不佳的经理，这些法律也会制约企业生产率，进而制约工人工资。

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:55.350
Indeed, in “An International Perspective on the New Zealand Productivity Paradox” (2014), the Productivity Commission singled out the low quality of managerial capabilities as a cause of the country’s poor productivity growth record.
事实上，生产力委员会在《从国际视角看新西兰生产率悖论》（2014年）中特别指出，管理能力水平低下是该国生产率增长一直表现不佳的原因之一。

00:01:56.150 --> 00:02:03.500
Nor are highly paid managers themselves immune from the harm caused by the ERA’s unjustified dismissal procedures.
《雇佣关系法》中针对无正当理由解雇的程序会造成伤害，高薪经理自身也无法免受其害。

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:11.700
Because employment protection laws make it costlier to fire an employee, employers are more cautious about hiring new staff.
由于就业保护法使解雇雇员的代价更高，雇主在招聘新员工时会更加谨慎。

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:16.190
This makes it harder for the marginal manager to gain employment.
这使得处于录用边缘的经理更难找到工作。

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:22.510
And firms pay staff less because firms carry the burden of the employment arrangement going wrong.
而且，雇佣安排一旦出问题，负担要由企业承担，因此企业付给员工的工资会更低。

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:26.880
Society also suffers from excessive employment protections.
社会也会因过度的就业保护而蒙受损害。

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:35.340
Stringent job dismissal regulations adversely affect productivity growth and hamper both prosperity and overall well-being.
严格的解雇规定会对生产率增长产生不利影响，既妨碍繁荣，又妨碍整体福祉。

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:48.780
Across the Tasman, Australia deals with the unjustified dismissal paradox by excluding employees earning above a specified “high-income threshold” from the protection of its unfair dismissal laws.
在塔斯曼海对岸，澳大利亚应对这一无正当理由解雇悖论的办法，是把收入高于规定“高收入门槛”的雇员排除在其不公平解雇法的保护之外。

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:59.390
In New Zealand, a 2016 private members’ Bill tried to permit firms and high-income employees to contract out of the unjustified dismissal regime.
在新西兰，2016年的一项议员个人法案曾试图允许企业和高收入雇员通过合同约定不适用无正当理由解雇制度。

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:08.030
However, the mechanisms proposed were unwieldy and the Bill was voted down following the change in government in 2017.
然而，法案提出的机制繁琐难行，2017年政府更迭后，该法案被投票否决。
